== Usage Examples ==
Here are a few examples showing how to use the template for different platforms:

<pre>
 <table>
  <tr>
    <td>{{sl|amazon|amazonid|Limited Edition}}</td>
    <td>{{sl|booth|2592696|relu|JP}}</td>
    <td>{{sl|amazonmusic|amazonmusicalbumid|Limited Edition}}</td>
    <td>{{sl|amazonmusicjp|amazonmusicalbumid|Limited Edition}}</td>
    <td>{{sl|spotify|spotifyalbumid|Limited Edition}}</td>
    <td>{{sl|spotify-track|spotifytrackid|Regular Edition}}</td>
    <td>{{sl|yt|ytvideoid|MV}}</td>
    <td>{{sl|animate-intl|productid|description|intl}}</td>
  </tr>
 </table>
</pre>
...results in:
<table>
<tr>
<td>{{sl|amazon|amazonid|Limited Edition}}</td>
<td>{{sl|booth|2592696|relu|JP}}</td>
<td>{{sl|amazonmusic|amazonmusicalbumid|Limited Edition}}</td>
<td>{{sl|amazonmusicjp|amazonmusicalbumid|Limited Edition}}</td>
<td>{{sl|spotify|spotifyalbumid|Limited Edition}}</td>
<td>{{sl|spotify-track|spotifytrackid|Regular Edition}}</td>
<td>{{sl|yt|ytvideoid|MV}}</td>
<td>{{sl|animate-intl|productid|description|intl}}</td>
<td>{{sl|universal|tyct39095}}</td>
</tr>
</table>
<small style='color:red'>
For booth link, for example, if the link is https://relu.booth.pm/items/2592696, the format is: <pre>{{sl|booth|2592696|relu|JP}}</pre>
<ol>
<li>The zeroth index will always be the 'l' template (lowercase 'L').</li>
<li>The first index is 'booth'.</li>
<li>The second index is the product ID, in this case, '2592696'.</li>
<li>The third index is the subdomain of the booth, here it is 'relu'.</li>
<li>The last index will be 'JP' if it is specific to Japan; otherwise, it is left blank for international.</li>
<li>Sorry for the inconvenience, but there is no index for description in this format for now just for booth shop template.</li>
</ol>
</small>

This concludes the documentation for the template. It’s designed to be flexible, supporting various platforms and use cases, while maintaining a clean and user-friendly design.
